# Microsoft Enterprise Dependency Injection

## Enterprise Container Setup

All services registered in [container.ts](mdc:src/infrastructure/di/container.ts) following **Microsoft enterprise DI patterns**.

## Enterprise Service Registration

```typescript
// In container.ts - Microsoft enterprise DI
container.registerSingleton('ServiceName', ServiceClass);
```

## Service Definition

```typescript
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';

@injectable()
export class MyService {
  constructor(@inject('DependencyName') private readonly dependency: DependencyType) {}
}
```

## Resolution

```typescript
// In non-injectable code
import { DIContainer } from './infrastructure/di/container';

const service = DIContainer.resolve<ServiceType>('ServiceName');
```

## Rules

- ✅ Use `@injectable()` decorator on all services
- ✅ Use `@inject('TokenName')` for dependencies
- ✅ Register all services as singletons
- ✅ Import `reflect-metadata` at app entry point
- ❌ Don't use `new ServiceClass()` directly in business logic
